WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.540
Karl Marx, a German philosopher, called
religion the opium of the people.

2
00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:07.010
He was an atheist.

3
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:10.840
He expected religion to
disappear once oppression ended.

4
00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:15.840
Yet Catholic liberation theologians in
Latin America borrowed some of his tools,

5
00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:18.810
to analyse why the poor stay poor.

6
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.700
Priests using an atheist's ideas?

7
00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.460
Rome took notice.

8
00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:26.110
So how did the Catholic Church respond?

9
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.130
In this mission, you'll learn
Marx's idea of exploitation:

10
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.500
who gains from a worker's labour.

11
00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.830
Then you'll read what
the Vatican said in 1984,

12
00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.340
and follow what changed after it.

13
00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:42.810
Your mission: find out how the Catholic
Church responded when its theologians

14
00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.280
borrowed from Marx.
